{
  "schema": "prova.verification-case/1",
  "title": "Network comparison test (permutation)",
  "description": "The network comparison test of two independent groups (n = 120 each, five variables; the package's fixture configuration 1): EBIC glasso networks at gamma = 0.5, absolute weighted differences, 15 permutations after set.seed(1). The reference is NetworkComparisonTest::NCT() on the same data and seed, kept in tests/testthat/fixtures/nct-reference.rds (the reference package is not installed here, so its side is retained, not rerun). With the same seed both draw the same permutations, so the p-values are comparable one to one. The fixture holds edge p-values in NCT's edge order (upper triangle, column by column), which is the order psychnets reports.",
  "covers": [
    "net_compare()"
  ],
